    "event": "Flood Warning",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Phoenix AZ",
    "headline": "Flood Warning issued November 7 at 10:25AM MST until November 8 at 11:00PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Maricopa County in south central Arizona...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1100 PM MST Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of the Verde River between Fort McDowell and the\nSalt River is occurring. Recreation on or near the Verde River will\nbe unsafe.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1025 AM MST, A streamflow gauge on the Verde River near the\nSalt River ",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nFlooding is occurring. It is important to know where you are relative\nto streams, rivers, or creeks. Campers and hikers should avoid\nstreams or creeks.",
    "response": "Avoid",
    "note": null,
