    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Seattle WA",
    "headline": "High Wind Warning issued November 7 at 1:17PM PST until November 8 at 4:00AM PST by NWS Seattle WA",
    "description": "* WHAT...South winds 25 to 35 mph with gusts up to 60 mph expected.\n\n* WHERE...Grays Harbor County Coast and Northern Washington Coast.\n\n* WHEN...Until 4 AM PST Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Damaging winds will blow down trees and power lines.\nWidespread power outages are expected. Travel will be difficult,\nespecially for high profile vehicles.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Strongest winds will be this evening.",
    "instruction": "People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around\nor damaged by the wind.",
    "response": "Prepare",
